# The API image builds from the repo root so it can see packages/. BuildKit picks this file up
# because it sits next to the dockerfile, and it REPLACES the root .dockerignore for this build.
# Allowlist only what the build reads; everything else (the web app, node_modules, .git, docs,
# scripts, the test projects, the KB CLI) stays out.
*
!Directory.Build.props
!apps/TakeInitiative.Api/
# The two packages the API has a ProjectReference to. KnowledgeBase arrived with 26c and was NOT
# added here, which broke the image outright: restore skipped the missing project and the publish
# failed on `CS0234: the type or namespace name 'KnowledgeBase' does not exist`. A new
# ProjectReference means a new line here.
!packages/TakeInitiative.Dice/
!packages/TakeInitiative.KnowledgeBase/

# global.json is deliberately absent: the sdk:10.0 image brings its own SDK, and pinning 10.0.400
# with rollForward=latestFeature would make the build fail the day that tag moves to 10.1.

# Build output and editor droppings inside the allowlisted trees. bin/ alone is a gigabyte locally.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
